llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: a zero-extending load of an i1 masks the byte (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a load of an i1 from memory,
which GlobalOpt makes of an internal bool global that is only ever
stored true and false. Upstream 4.0.0 (since 3.9) selects the
zero-extending load as a bare byte load, trusting the upper bits; the
PS4 compiler that built the game region kept LLVM 3.7's selection
patterns (X86InstrCompiler.td, "zextload bool -> zextload byte"): the
loaded byte is masked with `and 1`, at i8 (`mov al, [rip+x]; and al,
1`, the short AL form) or at i32 with the 32-bit immediate (`movzx eax,
byte [rip+x]; and eax, 1` encoded 25 01 00 00 00, or 81 /4 with another
register). LLVM 3.8 used the 8-bit-immediate AND for the wider forms
(83 /4 01); the base has none of those after such a load. Measured over
the game region (docs/NOTES.md, round 114A): the 45 loads of the 20
byte globals that are stored only with constant 0 and 1 and never have
their address taken are all masked in these forms (22 at i8, 23 at
i32), and none is loaded without the mask; the unmasked byte loads of
the region (11,994, `test al, al`) are on globals whose address is
taken (the function-local static guards). With this patch 0xb108d0
compiles to the base's bytes.

--- a/lib/Target/X86/X86InstrCompiler.td
+++ b/lib/Target/X86/X86InstrCompiler.td
@@ -1191,13 +1191,15 @@
 defm : CMOVmr<X86_COND_NO, CMOVO16rm , CMOVO32rm , CMOVO64rm>;
 
 // zextload bool -> zextload byte
-// i1 stored in one byte in zero-extended form.
-// Upper bits cleanup should be executed before Store.
-def : Pat<(zextloadi8i1  addr:$src), (MOV8rm addr:$src)>;
-def : Pat<(zextloadi16i1 addr:$src), (MOVZX16rm8 addr:$src)>;
-def : Pat<(zextloadi32i1 addr:$src), (MOVZX32rm8 addr:$src)>;
+// PS4: an i1 in memory is not trusted to be zero-extended; the loaded byte
+// is masked to its low bit, as LLVM 3.7 selected it (3.8 used the
+// 8-bit-immediate forms for the wider ANDs).
+def : Pat<(zextloadi8i1  addr:$src), (AND8ri (MOV8rm addr:$src), (i8 1))>;
+def : Pat<(zextloadi16i1 addr:$src), (AND16ri (MOVZX16rm8 addr:$src), (i16 1))>;
+def : Pat<(zextloadi32i1 addr:$src), (AND32ri (MOVZX32rm8 addr:$src), (i32 1))>;
 def : Pat<(zextloadi64i1 addr:$src),
-          (SUBREG_TO_REG (i64 0), (MOVZX32rm8 addr:$src), sub_32bit)>;
+          (SUBREG_TO_REG (i64 0),
+           (AND32ri (MOVZX32rm8 addr:$src), (i32 1)), sub_32bit)>;
 
 // extload bool -> extload byte
 // When extloading from 16-bit and smaller memory locations into 64-bit
